---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="Terms of service and usage conditions for AirPDF."
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 tracking-tight mb-4">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mb-8">Last revised: October 5, 2026</p>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
        <p>By accessing and utilizing AirPDF, you agree to comply with and be bound by these Terms of Service. If you disagree with any segment of these terms, you should discontinue using our website.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">2. Permitted Use</h2>
        <p>AirPDF provides free, client-side browser utilities for manipulating document files. You agree to use the service only for lawful purposes and in accordance with applicable local, national, and international laws.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">3. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
        <p>The service is provided on an "AS IS" and "AS AVAILABLE" basis. While we strive to deliver robust client-side algorithms, AirPDF makes no warranties, expressed or implied, regarding reliability, data integrity, or fitness for a particular purpose.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">4. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>In no event shall AirPDF or its maintainers be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, or consequential damages resulting from the use or inability to use our tools.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
